 "visual_audit": "Frame-0 montages for both conditions rendered and inspected by eye for v3b. All 15 FACE clips open on a clear frontal face; all 15 NONFACE clips show people with no dominant frontal face. Frame 0 is audited specifically because it is the over-weighted frame (17.0%).",
 "residual": [
  "The face-absent baseline still contains people and scenes rather than objects or scrambled controls, so 'face-absent' means 'something else', as in any localiser.",
  "Category labels rest on Haar cascades plus a visual audit, not hand-labelled ground truth.",
  "Power is unchanged by matching: still ~0.46 at AUC 0.70, so AMBIGUOUS remains a live outcome."
 ],
 "revision": "v3b (2026-07-30) REPLACES the first v3 selection pushed earlier the same day. The v3 selection was matched on motion estimated from a 160px full-film scan, but the acceptance criterion is evaluated on the delivered 480p clips. On those files v3 gave motion AUC 0.631, i.e. |AUC-0.5| = 0.131 against its own stated cap of 0.10 \u2014 it FAILED its own criterion. The p-value leg (0.246) passed, which is how it went unnoticed. v3b fixes the root cause: every one of the 42 shot representatives is cut at 480p and measured with the SAME estimator used for verification, and the selection then optimises the quantity the criterion actually measures.",
 "v_jepa2_window": "CORRECTION to an earlier claim in this project's record. V-JEPA2 does NOT clamp to the first 4 s. It slides a 4 s window: 20 stimulus bins at t = 0.5 .. 10.0 s x 64 frames = 1280 frames, so the encoder sees ALL TEN SECONDS in 20 overlapping spans. Frames sampled from before the clip start are clamped to frame 0 and number exactly 217 (55+47+39+31+23+15+7 for bins t=0.5..3.5). Both 1280 and 217 reproduce exactly under this reading and neither under a clamp reading (a true clamp would feed 64 frames). So frame 0 IS over-weighted, at 217/1280 = 17.0%, which is why the frame-0 selection clause and the frame-0 visual audit are kept \u2014 but the statement that the model 'only sees the first 4 s' was wrong and is withdrawn.",
